ns1:PGO-00000001 a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "assay"@en ;
    dcterms:description "**Round 1** (2025-05-08) The session aimed to reach consensus on the appropriate ontological definition for the concept \"Assay\" (or \"Bioassay\") within PGO, and to settle the preferred label. A key conceptual discussion clarified the semantic boundaries between related terms: **Assay** — a planned process measuring a specific activity or property (biological, chemical, physicochemical, sequence-based), typically following a defined protocol. **Experiment** — a broader, less formalized concept that may include multiple assays. **Study** — may encompass multiple experiments or be used synonymously with experiment. **Run** — repeated executions of the same assay or experiment. **Bioassay** — a subset of assays involving biological materials, reagents, or measuring biological properties. **Test** — sometimes used interchangeably with assay in regulatory/pharmacopeial contexts. Four candidate definitions were evaluated: 1. **OBI_0000070** (\"A planned process with the objective to produce information about the material entity that is the evaluant, by physically examining it or its proxies.\") — considered sufficiently flexible and formally grounded. Ultimately adopted. 2. **NCIT_C16341** (Bioassay) — positively received by multiple experts (Peter McQuilton, Birgit Meldal) for comprehensiveness but links to the PGO concept \"Substance\", creating potential circular dependency. 3. **BAO_15** — proposed by 2+ partners; criticized as overly complex and including SOP-level information. 4. **NCIT_C60819** — considered too narrow, limited to amount or drug-effect measurement. The group also resolved the label question: **\"Assay\"** is preferred over \"Bioassay\" or \"Assay/Bioassay\" for clarity and generality. \"Bioassay\" may be considered as a separate concept in future PGO versions. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on OBI_0000070 as the preferred definition with the label \"Assay\". Formal recommendation submitted to the Steering Group."@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "PGO-00000001" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:rights "OBI is maintained by the OBI Consortium and released under CC BY 4.0. https://obi-ontology.org/"@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://ontology.iedb.org/ontology/OBI:0000070> ;
    skos:altLabel "bioassay"@en,
        "experiment"@en,
        "observation"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <http://hl7.org/fhir/observation>,
        <https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/ClinicalMeasurement>,
        <https://bioschemas.org/LabProcess>,
        schema:MedicalTest,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q864212> ;
    skos:broader ns1:PGO-00000000 ;
    skos:definition "A planned process with the objective to produce information about the material entity that is the evaluant, by physically examining it or its proxies."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Assay: A qualitative or quantitative analysis performed to determine the amount of a particular constituent in a sample or the biological or pharmacological properties of a drug. [https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C60819]"@en,
        "BioAssay: A set of instructions, methodology, operations, required reagents, instruments to carry out experiments for the purpose of testing the effect of a perturbing agent in a biological model system, measuring one or multiple effect(s)... [https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/bao/classes/http%3A%2F%2Fwww.bioassayontology.org%2Fbao%23BAO_0000015]"@en,
        "Bioassay: A laboratory test or analysis of the biological activity of a substance performed by studying its effect on an organism or in a test tube under controlled conditions. [https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C16341]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000070>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q739897> ;
    skos:example [ dcterms:description "Assay quantifying interactions between two molecules (small molecule-protein, protein-protein, protein-DNA, etc.); BAO drug-discovery assay term, a child of bioassay (BAO_0000015)"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <http://www.bioassayontology.org/bao#BAO_0002989> ;
            rdf:value "binding assay" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "BAO" ],
        [ dcterms:description "Polymerase Chain Reaction Single Strand Conformation assay"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0302737> ;
            rdf:value "PCR-SSCP assay" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "OBI" ],
        [ dcterms:description "Enzyme-linked immunosorbent assay; widely used immunoassay in pharma R&D; OBI_0000661"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000661> ;
            rdf:value "ELISA" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "OBI" ],
        [ dcterms:description "A laboratory test measuring the ability of immune cells (cytotoxic T cells, NK cells) to kill target cells; MAXO clinical-domain assay (MAXO_0020017)"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0020017> ;
            rdf:value "cytotoxicity assay" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "MAXO" ],
        [ dcterms:description "A test to determine if cells are undergoing programmed cell death"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0035080> ;
            rdf:value "apoptosis assay" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "MAXO" ],
        [ dcterms:description "An assay to assess the presence of immune complexes in the blood circulation; MAXO clinical-domain assay (MAXO_0035109)"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MAXO_0035109> ;
            rdf:value "immune complex assay" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "MAXO" ],
        [ dcterms:description "ADP-ribose-specific chromatin-affinity purification; EFO assay term (EFO_0010012); illustrates EFO for assay annotation"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <http://www.ebi.ac.uk/efo/EFO_0010012> ;
            rdf:value "ADPr-ChAP" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "EFO" ] ;
    skos:inScheme ns1:PGOConceptScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "assay"@en ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2025-06-12"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-11-24"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:used "2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md",
        "2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md" ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo "pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py" ;
