ns1:PGO-00000005 a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "clinical study"@en ;
    dcterms:description "**Round 1** (2024-07-03) The session established initial consensus around NCIT C15206. Key discussion points: **Common identifier source**: AstraZeneca emphasised the importance of agreeing on which identifier source to use for clinical trials to avoid ambiguity in cross-system referencing. **Resolution services**: GSK proposed a preference hierarchy for resolution services (e.g., identifiers.org first, then alternatives). This was noted for future preferred-sources discussion. **Preference for original source text**: Merck KGaA expressed a preference for using the definition text exactly as found in the original reference resource. This position was unanimously endorsed and adopted as a guiding principle for PGO definitions generally. **Outcome:** Initial consensus on NCIT C15206. Follow-up session scheduled to address ClinOps alignment. **Round 2** (2024-08-01) This session addressed input from the Pistoia Alliance ClinOps group (GitHub issue #34), which utilises the USDM (Unified Study Definition Model) definition: *\"involves research using human volunteers (also called participants) that is intended to add to medical knowledge.\"* The expert group concluded that: 1. The USDM/ClinOps definition is not in conflict with NCIT_C15206; the NCIT definition is broader but compatible. 2. The second part of the NCIT definition (\"includes development of new technologies, study of mechanisms of human diseases...\") was viewed as descriptive commentary rather than essential semantic content. 3. The terminological equivalence of \"human subject\", \"volunteer\", and \"participant\" was acknowledged as an open point but not a critical obstacle to adoption. **Outcome:** Confirmed consensus on NCIT_C15206. GitHub issue #34 resolved. Formal recommendation submitted to the Steering Group."@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "PGO-00000005" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:rights "\"NCI THESAURUS™ is released under CC BY 4.0. Produced by the Enterprise Vocabulary Services group, National Cancer Institute, Maryland, USA.\""@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C15206> ;
    skos:altLabel "clinical study"@en,
        "clinical trial"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <http://hl7.org/fhir/ResearchStudy>,
        <https://bioschemas.org/Study>,
        schema:MedicalTrial ;
    skos:broader ns1:PGO-00000000 ;
    skos:definition "Research conducted with human subjects or on material of human origin in which an investigator directly interacts with human subjects; includes development of new technologies, study of mechanisms of human diseases, therapy, clinical trials, epidemiologic, behavior, and health services research."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Clinical Study: A work that reports on the results of a research study to evaluate interventions or exposures on biomedical or health-related outcomes. The two main types of clinical studies are interventional studies (clinical trials) and observational studies. [http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D000068397]"@en,
        "Medical Trial: A medical trial is a type of medical study that uses a scientific process to compare the safety and efficacy of medical therapies or medical procedures. [https://schema.org/MedicalTrial]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C15206>,
        <https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/ClinicalTrial>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q30612> ;
    skos:example [ dcterms:description "Japanese trial (jRCT): Phase 2, randomized, placebo-controlled study of SAR448851 in participants with early Alzheimer's disease"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://jrct.mhlw.go.jp/en-latest-detail/jRCT2061260062> ;
            rdf:value "jRCT2061260062" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "jRCT" ],
        [ dcterms:description "WHO ICTRP record aggregating a Chinese (ChiCTR) trial not listed as a separate PGO source: sequential mepolizumab/stapokibart therapy for CRSwNP with severe eosinophilic asthma; illustrates ICTRP's meta-registry value"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://trialsearch.who.int/Trial2.aspx?TrialID=ChiCTR2600127395> ;
            rdf:value "ChiCTR2600127395 (via WHO ICTRP)" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "WHO ICTRP" ],
        [ dcterms:description "UK trial (ISRCTN registry): effect of inhaled-steroid non-adherence on response to mepolizumab in severe asthma"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://www.isrctn.com/ISRCTN10555748> ;
            rdf:value "ISRCTN10555748" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "ISRCTN" ],
        [ dcterms:description "Australian trial (ANZCTR, a WHO ICTRP primary registry): bacterial mucosal immunotherapy to prevent lower respiratory tract infections in preterm infants"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://www.anzctr.org.au/Trial/Registration/TrialReview.aspx?id=390988> ;
            rdf:value "ACTRN12626001111369 (BALLOON-AU)" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "ANZCTR" ],
        [ dcterms:description "Phase 3 imaging study ([123I]NAV5001) for the diagnosis of parkinsonian syndromes"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT01950455> ;
            rdf:value "NCT01950455" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "ClinicalTrials.gov" ],
        [ dcterms:description "COMMIT trial: efficacy and safety of adding clopidogrel to aspirin, or metoprolol, in acute myocardial infarction; direct ClinicalTrials.gov link"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT00222573> ;
            rdf:value "NCT00222573" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "ClinicalTrials.gov" ] ;
    skos:inScheme ns1:PGOConceptScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "clinical study"@en ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2025-03-12"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-11-24"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:used "2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md",
        "2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md" ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo "pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py" ;
