ns1:PGO-00000006 a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "clinical study site"@en ;
    dcterms:description "**Round 1** (2025-01-30) The session revealed significant conceptual complexity around the term \"site\", which spans anatomical, geographic, institutional, and procedural domains. Experts distinguished between a high-level generic concept and more context-specific subtypes. Key findings: **BFO_0000029 (Site)**: Philosophically rigorous but too abstract for practical PGO implementation. Some experts appreciated its generality; others considered it impractical. **OMG Site definition** (\"place, setting, or context in which something is situated or to which something is, or may be, bound\") was generally preferred by experts for its clarity and pragmatic scope — however, the IRI is unresolvable (issue #48), blocking immediate adoption. **NCIT_C70777 (Clinical Study Site)**: Strongly endorsed for representing real-world entities engaged in clinical research. The experts recommended a stratified approach: 1. A generic \"Site\" — pending a resolvable URI for the OMG definition. 2. \"Clinical_Study_Site\" (NCIT_C70777) — adopt for Phase 1. 3. Additional Phase 2 concepts: \"Study_Site\", \"Anatomical_Site\", \"Binding_Site\". **Outcome:** Further update required to confirm OMG IRI status and finalise the pragmatic recommendation. **Round 2** (2025-05-28) Follow-up confirmed that the OMG IRI issue (#48) could not be resolved: OMG IRIs are not currently resolvable, per input from Asiyah Yu Lin (Pistoia Alliance). As a consequence, the OMG \"Site\" definition cannot be used for PGO at this time. The pragmatic proposal for Phase 1: 1. Defer a generic \"Site\" definition until a resolvable and implementable URI is available. 2. Adopt \"Clinical_Study_Site\" with NCIT_C70777 as the Phase 1 core concept. 3. Flag additional Phase 2 sub-concepts for subsequent alignment. **Outcome:** Final recommendation confirmed. Submitted to Steering Group."@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "PGO-00000006" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:rights "\"NCI THESAURUS™ is released under CC BY 4.0. Produced by the Enterprise Vocabulary Services group, National Cancer Institute, Maryland, USA.\""@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C70777> ;
    skos:broadMatch <https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/Site>,
        schema:MedicalOrganization,
        schema:Place,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q57951700> ;
    skos:broader ns1:PGO-00000000 ;
    skos:definition "A healthcare organization, an institution, a facility, a healthcare provider, or a part or a constituent of any of the above entities directly involved in conducting a particular clinical study."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Site: A place, setting, or context in which something is situated or to which something is, or may be, bound. [https://www.omg.org/spec/Commons/20250201/Facilities/Site]"@en,
        "Study Site: A facility in which study/protocol activities are conducted. [https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C80403]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C70777>,
        <http://snomed.info/id/394577000> ;
    skos:example [ dcterms:description "Clinical study site in Basel, Switzerland"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://clinicaltrials.gov/study/NCT07015567?locStr=Basel,%20Switzerland&country=Switzerland&state=Basel%20City&city=Basel&rank=1#locations> ;
            rdf:value "Basel, BS, Switzerland — UPK Transkulturelle Ambulanz" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "ClinicalTrials.gov" ] ;
    skos:inScheme ns1:PGOConceptScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "clinical study site"@en ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2025-06-12"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-11-24"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:used "2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md",
        "2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md" ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo "pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py" ;
