ns1:PGO-00000007 a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "compound"@en ;
    dcterms:description "**Round 1** (2025-03-06) The session jointly evaluated \"Compound\" and \"Substance\" to clarify their conceptual relationship. Key findings: \"Compound\" appears to have a more precise, accurate chemical composition than \"Substance\"; \"Chemical compound\" was noted as a possibly more accurate label but compatible with NCIT_C43366. The semantic boundaries between \"compound\", \"substance\", \"drug\", and \"product\" were acknowledged as context-dependent and partially overlapping. Initial convergence on NCIT_C43366 as the least controversial definition. **Outcome:** Initial consensus on NCIT_C43366. Follow-up session scheduled. **Round 2** (2025-03-25) The round 2 session confirmed NCIT_C43366 as the least controversial candidate. The group acknowledged the definition is not ideal — \"substance\", \"element\", and \"ingredient\" are imprecise terms — but no better candidate with a resolvable identifier and permissive licence was identified. The label \"compound\" was confirmed as appropriate (over \"chemical compound\"), aligned with common pharma R&D usage. The group also discussed examples to illustrate the distinction between compound, drug, and product: acetylsalicylic acid (as compound) vs. aspirin (as product) acetaminophen (as compound) vs. paracetamol (as product) semaglutide (as compound/drug) **Outcome:** Consensus confirmed on NCIT_C43366. Recommendation submitted to Steering Group."@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "PGO-00000007" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:rights "\"NCI THESAURUS™ is released under CC BY 4.0. Produced by the Enterprise Vocabulary Services group, National Cancer Institute, Maryland, USA.\""@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C43366> ;
    skos:altLabel "chemical"@en,
        "chemical compound"@en,
        "chemical substance"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <http://hl7.org/fhir/Substance>,
        <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/CHEBI_24431>,
        <https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/ChemicalSubstance> ;
    skos:broader ns1:PGO-00000000 ;
    skos:definition "A substance formed by chemical union of two or more elements or ingredients in definite proportion by weight."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Chemical substance: A chemical substance is a portion of matter of constant composition, composed of molecular entities of the same type or of different types. [https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:59999]"@en,
        "Substances_Hydrate: Description of the addition of a compound (substance) that contains water in weak chemical combination with another compound [https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/idmp/ontology/ISO/ISO11238-Substances/Hydrate]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C43366>,
        <https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/ChemicalEntity>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11173> ;
    skos:example [ dcterms:description "Simple organic compound; CAS RN 64-17-5 (in the free CAS Common Chemistry subset)"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://commonchemistry.cas.org/detail?cas_rn=64-17-5> ;
            rdf:value "ethanol" ;
