ns1:PGO-00000008 a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "device"@en ;
    dcterms:description "**Round 1** (2025-02-13) There is a need for a broad \"device\" core concept in pharma R&ED. The variety of devices deployed in pharma is enormous, so context is important. Key discussion points: \"Device\" makes sense as a high-level entry-point label; covers laboratory equipment, production equipment, diagnostic tools, and medical devices. NCIT_C62103 (*\"An object contrived for a specific purpose\"*) was considered pragmatically appropriate despite some concern about breadth. An additional option was noted: NCIT_C19238 (*\"A manufactured object used to perform diagnostic, therapeutic or research activities\"*) — would exclude manufacturing equipment. IDMP-O's \"medical device\" definition is appropriate as a future sub-concept child class. The group reached consensus on NCIT_C62103 for the Phase 1 \"device\" concept, with three sub-concepts recommended for Phase 2: \"Instrument\" — laboratory/measurement device for scientific investigation \"Medical device\" — e.g. NCIT_C16830 \"Manufacturing equipment\" — tablet manufacturing device (out of scope for R&ED extension) GitHub issue #37 remains open pending a formal label decision in the PGO repository. **Outcome:** Consensus on NCIT_C62103. Recommendation submitted to Steering Group."@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "PGO-00000008" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:rights "\"NCI THESAURUS™ is released under CC BY 4.0. Produced by the Enterprise Vocabulary Services group, National Cancer Institute, Maryland, USA.\""@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C62103> ;
    skos:altLabel "instrument"@en,
        "laboratory instrument"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <http://hl7.org/fhir/Device>,
        <https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/Device>,
        <https://bioschemas.org/Thing>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6554101> ;
    skos:broader ns1:PGO-00000000 ;
    skos:definition "An object contrived for a specific purpose. OR: An object that has a specific use. In medicine, wheelchairs, pumps, and artificial limbs are examples of devices."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Medical Device: Any physical object that is useful for prevention, diagnosis, monitoring, or treatment of disease or other conditions. [https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C16830]"@en,
        "device: A material entity that is designed to perform a function in a scientific investigation, but is not a reagent. [http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000968]"@en,
        "medical device: Specification of an instrument, apparatus, appliance, software, material or other article ... not achieve its principal intended action by pharmacological, immunological or metabolic means ... [https://spec.pistoiaalliance.org/idmp/ontology/ISO/ISO11615-MedicinalProducts/MedicalDevice]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C62103>,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q6554101> ;
    skos:example [ dcterms:description "Instrument used to separate mixture components by density"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0400106> ;
            rdf:value "centrifuge" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "OBI" ],
        [ dcterms:description "Instrument used to perform the polymerase chain reaction (PCR machine); OBI_0000989 (click-verified by GN 2026-10-17)"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OBI_0000989> ;
            rdf:value "PCR instrument" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "OBI" ] ;
    skos:inScheme ns1:PGOConceptScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "device"@en ;
