ns1:PGO-00000018 a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "adverse event"@en ;
    dcterms:description "**Round 1** (2025-10-16) The session (2025-10-16) focused on Adverse Event as the primary concept (Medical Device was also discussed — separate record another concept). The group reviewed approximately 10 candidate definitions, removing exact duplicates during the call. The shortlist converged on two candidates: OAE_0000001 and NCIT C41331. OAE_0000001 was judged concise and from an authoritative dedicated ontology for adverse events, but noted as potentially limited in scope and not updated since 2022. NCIT C41331 was preferred by the group for its content richness — it covers drug-drug interactions (noted by an expert: \"takes into account drug-drug interaction as well\"), applies across clinical, regulatory, and post-market contexts, and is from a highly trusted, broadly used source. Darko noted NCIT definitions are generally \"wordy\" but agreed on content quality. Process issues also discussed: URL policy established: definitions must point to the original source organization, not BioPortal. BioPortal is acceptable for discovery but not as the primary citation. Ammar added SIDER (http://sideeffects.embl.de/) as an example resource for Adverse Event during the call. A \"meta-level\" context label (R&D vs. clinical) was requested by Chris Day and an expert, but noted by Giovanni as requiring an agreed pharma meta-model not yet available. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on NCIT C41331 as the preferred definition with the label `Adverse_Event`. Formal recommendation submitted to Steering Group."@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "PGO-00000018" ;
    dcterms:license <http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dcterms:rights "NCI Thesaurus, National Cancer Institute. Concept C41331. https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C41331"@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C41331> ;
    skos:altLabel "Adverse drug reaction"@en,
        "Adverse effect"@en,
        "Side effect"@en,
        "Unwanted effect"@en ;
    skos:broader ns1:PGO-00000000 ;
    skos:definition "Any unfavorable or unintended disease, sign, or symptom (including an abnormal laboratory finding) that is temporally associated with the use of a medical treatment or procedure, and that may or may not be considered related to the medical treatment or procedure."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Adverse Event Actuality: Overall nature of the adverse event, e.g. real or potential. [https://hl7.org/fhir/R5/codesystem-adverse-event-actuality.html]"@en,
        "Adverse Event: An unfavorable change in the health of a participant, including abnormal laboratory findings, that happens during a clinical study or within a certain period of time after the study. [https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/CTO-NDD]"@en,
        "Adverse Event: Pathologic Function type from UMLS [https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/MEDDRA]"@en,
        "AdverseEvent: An event that may be related to unintended effects on a patient or research participant. [https://www.hl7.org/fhir/adverseevent.html]"@en,
        "AdverseEvent: Any unfavorable and unintended sign, symptom, disease, or other medical occurrence with a temporal association with the use of a medical product, procedure, or other medical intervention. [https://bioportal.bioontology.org/ontologies/BRIDG]"@en,
        "Synonym 'Adverse drug reaction': AE subset"@en,
        "adverse effect: [Specification of] any potential undesirable side effect, adverse reaction or event, complication, or other similar potential consequence associated with the use of a medicinal product. [(URL not provided)]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C41331> ;
    skos:example [ dcterms:description "Common drug-induced adverse event (e.g. following chemotherapy)"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <http://sideeffects.embl.de/se/C0027497/> ;
            rdf:value "Nausea" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "SIDER 4.1" ],
        [ dcterms:description "MedDRA Preferred Term (PT 10028813)"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <http://purl.bioontology.org/ontology/MEDDRA/10028813> ;
            rdf:value "Nausea (MedDRA PT 10028813)" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "MedDRA" ],
        [ dcterms:description "Drug-induced liver injury — serious adverse event category"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <http://sideeffects.embl.de/se/C0235378/> ;
            rdf:value "Hepatotoxicity" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "SIDER 4.1" ] ;
    skos:inScheme ns1:PGOConceptScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "adverse event"@en ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-03-03"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-11-24"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:used "2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md",
        "2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md" ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo "pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py" ;
