ns1:PGO-00000020 a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "study site"@en ;
    dcterms:description "**Round 1** (2025-12-11) The session (2025-12-11) covered Site and Study_Site (both concepts discussed together given their parent-child relationship — Site record: another concept). For Study_Site, the group noted it adds necessary value as a non-clinical complement to Clinical_Study_Site (already in PGO V1.0). An expert confirmed relevance for preclinical settings. The key conceptual insight came from an expert and Christine: study sites must be **approved** — *\"you have to go through a process to get approval for a place to actually be a study site.\"* This \"approved\" qualifier was seen as fundamental: it distinguishes Study_Site from any arbitrary research location, reflects regulatory reality, and is absent from the NCIT facility-framing and CDISC investigator-framing alternatives. Three main NCIT-sourced definitions were reviewed: 1. NCIT C80403 primary formulation (\"A facility in which study/protocol activities are conducted\") — noted by Darko (from Phase 1 history) as too restrictive given \"facility\" scope. 2. CDISC formulation (\"The location at which a study investigator conducts study activities\") — rejected for requiring a named \"study investigator\" and being too study-agent-centric. 3. MRCT-Ctr formulation (\"An approved location where research study activities take place\") — preferred by an expert, an expert, and Christine for \"approved\" qualifier and broader \"research study\" (not \"clinical study\") scope. Giovanni: *\"Study site. This goes to light.\"* **Outcome:** Consensus reached on the NCIT C80403 / MRCT-Ctr formulation as the preferred definition. Label `Study_Site` confirmed."@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "PGO-00000020" ;
    dcterms:license <http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dcterms:rights "NCI Thesaurus, National Cancer Institute. Concept C80403. https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C80403"@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C80403> ;
    skos:altLabel "Investigation site"@en,
        "Research site"@en,
        "Trial site"@en ;
    skos:broadMatch <https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/Site>,
        schema:MedicalOrganization,
        schema:Place,
        <https://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q57951700> ;
    skos:broader ns1:PGO-00000000 ;
    skos:closeMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C70777>,
        <http://snomed.info/id/394577000> ;
    skos:definition "An approved location where research study activities take place."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Definition source: (MRCT-Ctr formulation)"@en,
        "Location: Details and position information for a place where services are provided and resources and participants may be stored, found, contained, or accommodated, and/or where activities may be performed. [https://build.fhir.org/location.html]"@en,
        "Place: Entities that have a somewhat fixed, physical extension. [https://schema.org/Place]"@en,
        "Site: (A position in relation to its surroundings) [NCIT_C37901]"@en,
        "Study Site: The location at which a study investigator conducts study activities. [CDISC (accessible via NCIT_C80403)]"@en,
        "Synonym 'Trial site': clinical context"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C80403> ;
    skos:example [ dcterms:description "FHIR Location resource instance representing a clinical study facility"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://build.fhir.org/location-example.html> ;
            rdf:value "Burgers Amsterdam South, South Wing 2nd floor" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "FHIR Location" ] ;
    skos:inScheme ns1:PGOConceptScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "study site"@en ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-03-03"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-11-24"^^xsd:date ;
