ns1:PGO-00000021 a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "medical condition"@en ;
    dcterms:description "**Round 1** (2025-11-14) The 2025-11-26 session (following initial discussion on 2025-11-14) reviewed seven candidate definitions. The central debate was the scope boundary between Disease and Medical_Condition: the expert group agreed that Medical_Condition must be broader than Disease, explicitly covering non-pathological conditions such as pregnancy, childbirth, and vaccination recommendations. Key discriminators discussed: (a) non-pathological inclusion — schema.org was criticised for missing this; (b) treatment vs. monitoring — NCIT C156809 was rejected for limiting to \"monitoring\"; (c) circularity — OPMI and GSSO second sentence were noted as incoherent. The GSSO:000485 definition was selected as the best available: Birgit Meldal proposed it; the group noted it as \"the most comprehensive\" and \"the best option identified.\" Its key advantages: broad scope including all diseases, lesions, disorders, AND non-pathological conditions; examples provided (pregnancy, childbirth); suggests the norm of medical treatment. Acknowledged weaknesses: the second sentence (\"Any kind of illness or circumstance which requires medical monitoring\") is less coherent than the first sentence and was noted as potentially restrictive (colour blindness does not require monitoring). However, these were not blocking. Alternative: schema.org MedicalCondition was supported by (Philippe Rocca-Serra) and partially by Ammar Ammar, but criticised for omitting non-pathological conditions and lacking the \"medical\" component. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on GSSO:000485 as the preferred definition. Label `Medical_Condition` confirmed."@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "PGO-00000021" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:rights "GSSO Ontology. Concept GSSO:000485 (medical condition). http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GSSO_000485"@en ;
    dcterms:source <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GSSO_000485> ;
    skos:altLabel "Condition"@en,
        "Health condition"@en,
        "Medical condition"@en ;
    skos:broader ns1:PGO-00000000 ;
    skos:definition "A broad term that includes all diseases, lesions, disorders, or nonpathologic condition that normally receives medical treatment, such as pregnancy or childbirth. Any kind of illness or circumstance which requires medical monitoring."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Disease or Phenotypic Feature: Either one of a disease or an individual phenotypic feature. [https://biolink.github.io/biolink-model/DiseaseOrPhenotypicFeature/]"@en,
        "Disease: A disease is a disposition to undergo pathological processes that exists in an organism because of one or more disorders in that organism. [http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MONDO_0000001]"@en,
        "Medical Condition: Any kind of illness or circumstance which requires medical monitoring. [NCIT:C156809]"@en,
        "Synonym 'Medical condition': capitalised as per schema.org"@en,
        "medical condition: The medical state or condition of a patient [OPMI:0000282]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/GSSO_000485> ;
    skos:example [ dcterms:description "Non-pathological medical condition — key example from GSSO definition"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C25742> ;
            rdf:value "Pregnancy" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "NCIT" ],
        [ dcterms:description "Common pathological medical condition"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C26747> ;
            rdf:value "Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "NCIT" ],
        [ dcterms:description "Rare hereditary medical condition; ORPHA:391665"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/391665> ;
            rdf:value "Homozygous familial hypercholesterolemia" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "Orphanet" ] ;
    skos:inScheme ns1:PGOConceptScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "medical condition"@en ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-03-03"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-11-24"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:used "2-PGO-templates/PGO-MD-output-template-v1.7.md",
        "2-PGO-templates/PGO-T-internal-record-template-v1.7.md" ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo "pgo_r_to_public_md.v1.10.0.py" ;
    ns1:preferredSource [ a void:Dataset ;
            dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
