ns1:PGO-00000022 a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "contraindication"@en ;
    dcterms:description "**Round 1** (2025-11-14) The session reviewed multiple candidate definitions for Contraindication, including sources from OAE, MeSH, NCIT, and ISO IDMP. The group examined the conceptual relationship between Contraindication and Adverse Event — explicitly distinguishing the two: an adverse event is what may occur, while a contraindication is the reason not to proceed with a treatment. The OAE definition (OAE_0000055) emerged as the clear preference: Darko Hric noted it offers \"more descriptive language than others while keeping it precise\"; Birgit Meldal agreed. The group acknowledged a mild wording issue — the phrase \"An contraindication\" contains a grammatical error (should be \"A contraindication\") and the definition has a degree of circularity — but these were deemed non-blocking. The MeSH definition (absolute/relative split) was considered but judged as less precise. The NCIT C50646 definition was noted as qualitatively good but would require a label change. The ISO IDMP definition was rejected for being too drug-centric. Post-session, the Steering Group confirmed the label as the single word \"contraindication\" (rejecting the hyphenated form \"contra-indication\") and requested an optional improvement: consider submitting an updated definition to OAE to reduce circularity. This optional action was flagged 2026-05-28; no status change was triggered. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on OAE OAE_0000055 as the preferred definition. Label `Contraindication` confirmed."@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "PGO-00000022" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:rights "Ontology of Adverse Events, OAE_0000055. http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000055"@en ;
    dcterms:source <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000055> ;
    skos:altLabel "Contra-indication"@en ;
    skos:broader ns1:PGO-00000000 ;
    skos:definition "A contraindication is a disposition that increases the risk of harm involved in using a particular drug, carrying out a medical procedure, or engaging in a particular activity such that the risk of harm exceeds a threshold. An contraindication serves as a reason to withhold a certain medical treatment."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Adverse Event (context): Any unfavorable or unintended disease, sign, or symptom … temporally associated with the use of a medical treatment. [NCIT:C41331]"@en,
        "Contraindication: situation where the medicinal product shall not be given for safety reasons [ISO IDMP]"@en,
        "Contraindications: A condition or factor associated with a recipient that makes the use of a drug, procedure, or physical agent improper or inadvisable. Contraindications may be absolute (life threatening) or relative (higher risk of complications in which benefits may outweigh risks). [http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D000075202]"@en,
        "Medical Contraindication: A symptom or medical condition that makes a particular treatment or procedure inadvisable because a person is likely to have a bad reaction. For example, having a bleeding disorder is a contraindication for taking aspirin because treatment with aspirin may cause excess bleeding. [https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C50646]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/OAE_0000055> ;
    skos:example [ dcterms:description "General medical contraindication concept; NCIt C50646"@en ;
