ns1:PGO-00000024 a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "bioassay"@en ;
    dcterms:description "**Round 1** (2025-11-14) The session reviewed six candidate definitions for Bioassay. The discussion established that Bioassay should be understood as a narrower child of Assay (PGO-00000001), with the key distinguishing feature being the biological substrate — the assay measures biological activity on a living organism or in a controlled in vitro system. The BAO and MMO definitions were challenged for reading as assay method definitions (describing how to run an assay) rather than definitions of what a bioassay is. The MIRO definition was criticized for limiting scope to organism effects only, excluding in vitro contexts. The MeSH definition suffered from the same method-framing problem. The NCIT C16341 definition — proposed by — was favoured as the clearest available option: it covers both in vivo (organism) and in vitro (test tube) scope, and is concise without over-specifying the method. Acknowledged limitations: \"test tube\" is an informal proxy for in vitro; the scope of one vs. multiple substances in a single assay was flagged as ambiguous but not blocking. The group noted that \"assay\" is always artificial (not in situ with a patient). Consensus was reached on NCIT C16341. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on NCIT C16341 as the preferred definition. Label `Bioassay` confirmed. Open discussion: \"an expert's input is key\" for any future refinement; precision on in vitro vs in vivo scope was flagged for potential improvement."@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "PGO-00000024" ;
    dcterms:license <http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/> ;
    dcterms:rights "NCI Thesaurus, National Cancer Institute. Concept C16341. https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C16341"@en ;
    dcterms:source <https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C16341> ;
    skos:altLabel "Biological assay"@en,
        "Biological test"@en ;
    skos:broader ns1:PGO-00000000 ;
    skos:definition "A laboratory test or analysis of the biological activity of a substance performed by studying its effect on an organism or in a test tube under controlled conditions."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Bioassay: A bioassay is a biological assay that consists of (…) a process that selects or identifies a (non-biological) perturbagen from a collection of perturbagens based on the effect on a biological entity. [http://www.bioassayontology.org/bao#BAO_0000015]"@en,
        "Bioassay: Any method of determining the concentration, relative activity, or effects of a biologically active substance in a sample by comparing its effect on an organism, tissue or cells with that of a reference standard. [http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/MMO_0000441]"@en,
        "Biological Assay: A method of measuring the effects of a biologically active substance using an intermediate in vivo or in vitro tissue or cell model under controlled conditions. [mesh:D001681]"@en,
        "Measured Bioassay: The direct processing of information in a physical bioAssay by the featureExtraction event. [NCIT:C44471]"@en,
        "bioassay: Bioassay is a shorthand commonly used term for biological assay and is a type of scientific experiment. Bioassays are typically conducted to measure the effects of a substance on a living organism. [MIRO:20000058]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch <http://purl.obolibrary.org/obo/NCIT_C16341> ;
    skos:example [ dcterms:description "Antibody-dependent cellular cytotoxicity bioassay for monoclonal antibody characterisation"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chembl/assay/CHEMBL2180721> ;
            rdf:value "ADCC reporter bioassay" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "ChEMBL" ],
        [ dcterms:description "Bioassay measuring inhibition of HIV replication in a cellular model"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/bioassay/1346982> ;
            rdf:value "HIV replication inhibition assay" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "PubChem BioAssay" ],
        [ dcterms:description "Bioassay measuring cell viability; BAO bioassay-branch term (child of bioassay BAO_0000015)"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <http://www.bioassayontology.org/bao#BAO_0003009> ;
            rdf:value "cell viability assay" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "BAO" ] ;
    skos:inScheme ns1:PGOConceptScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "bioassay"@en ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-05-13"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:generatedAtTime "2026-11-24"^^xsd:date ;
