ns1:PGO-00000027 a skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "medical indication"@en ;
    dcterms:description "**Round 1** (2025-11-14) The alignment sessions (2025-11-14 and 2025-11-26) explored the scope of Therapeutic/Medical Indication as a specialisation of Indication (PGO V1.0). The group noted that no single available definition was fully satisfactory: \"There is no fully satisfactory candidate. A combination of the wording from e.g. https://schema.org/MedicalIndication and e.g. https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q496997 would be preferred.\" The NCIT C41184 definition (already used for PGO V1.0 Indication) was excluded for re-use here. The EUPATI Toolbox definition was broadly rejected as drug-centric and lacking a persistent identifier. Wikipedia was qualitatively appreciated but rejected for instability. Schema.org MedicalIndication emerged as the preferred primary source: Ammar Ammar proposed it; an expert noted its conciseness; Birgit Meldal endorsed it for including risk factors (relevant for vaccine indications); an expert found it \"less verbose and more focused\"; Philippe Rocca-Serra and Ammar Ammar gave explicit +1. Wikidata Q496997 was strongly endorsed as a complementary framing (Birgit Meldal, Philippe Rocca-Serra) but was not selected as primary given stability concerns. A key label discussion emerged: the group strongly felt that \"Therapeutic_Indication\" is too narrow — it excludes diagnostic indications and prevention scenarios. The proposal to change the label to \"Medical_Indication\" was put forward during the 2025-11-26 session and confirmed by the SG at 2026-05-13 (ISSUE I-02). The meeting notes record: \"Medical Indication is broader than Therapeutic Indication.\" The relationship to PGO V1.0 Indication was discussed: Medical_Indication is likely a child entity of Indication, with a more specific therapy-oriented scope. This modelling point was not formally resolved at the expert level. **Outcome:** Consensus reached on schema.org MedicalIndication as the preferred definition. Label changed to `Medical_Indication`. SG approval: 2026-05-13. Editorial note: definition may need future refinement incorporating Wikidata Q496997 wording."@en ;
    dcterms:identifier "PGO-00000027" ;
    dcterms:license <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/> ;
    dcterms:rights "Schema.org. Term: MedicalIndication. https://schema.org/MedicalIndication"@en ;
    dcterms:source schema:MedicalIndication ;
    skos:altLabel "Clinical indication"@en,
        "Therapeutic indication"@en ;
    skos:broader ns1:PGO-00000000 ;
    skos:definition "A condition or factor that indicates use of a medical therapy, including signs, symptoms, risk factors, anatomical states, etc."@en ;
    skos:editorialNote "Indication: A sign, signal, circumstance, or symptom which serves to indicate or point out the cause, pathology, treatment, or issue of an attack of disease; the basis for initiation of a treatment for a disease or of a diagnostic test. [NCIT:C41184]"@en,
        "Therapeutic Indication: Therapeutic indications are a description of the disease to be treated with a medicine, and the population for which the medicine is intended. [EUPATI Toolbox (no persistent URI)]"@en ;
    skos:exactMatch schema:MedicalIndication ;
    skos:example [ dcterms:description "Prevention-based indication — not a disease; demonstrates scope beyond disease-centric definitions"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q84263196> ;
            rdf:value "Prevention of COVID-19 (vaccine indication)" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "Wikidata" ],
        [ dcterms:description "Oncology indication defined by molecular marker"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C53556> ;
            rdf:value "HER2-positive breast cancer (indication for trastuzumab)" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "NCIT" ],
        [ dcterms:description "Disease indication for a class of therapeutic agents"@en ;
            dcterms:identifier <https://evsexplore.semantics.cancer.gov/evsexplore/concept/ncit/C26747> ;
            rdf:value "Type 2 Diabetes Mellitus (indication for GLP-1 agonists)" ;
            prov:wasDerivedFrom "NCIT" ] ;
    skos:inScheme ns1:PGOConceptScheme ;
    skos:prefLabel "medical indication"@en ;
